opp	one
genopp	one
living_from_dead	one
souls_below	one
# opp: P1's examples are mostly comparatives with degrees (greater/less, stronger/weaker), while life/death look like all-or-nothing states.
# But S16 and S19 already count sleep/waking as opposites under the same principle, and life/death are treated as states of one subject in the same way.
# So I did not find two senses of "opposites" here.
# genopp / living_from_dead: "generated from the dead" could mean living beings arising out of dead matter, rather than one subject passing from one state to the other.
# S39's "whether things or persons" leaves this open, but I read every statement as the same subject changing state.
